So `opt_pin` and `opt_newpin` point to strings in argv. Now let me look at the `change_pin` function again. The key issue is:

```c
pincode = (u8 *) opt_pin;
if (pincode == NULL) {
    pincode = get_pin("Enter old PIN", pin_obj);
    if (!pinpad_present && pincode == NULL)
        return 2;
}
```

If `opt_pin` is NULL and `pinpad_present` is true, `get_pin` returns NULL (if `opt_use_pinpad` is set), and we continue with `pincode == NULL`.

Then:
```c
if (pincode && strlen((char *) pincode) == 0) {
    fprintf(stderr, "No PIN code supplied.\n");
    free(pincode);
    return 2;
}
```

Skipped.

```c
newpin = (u8 *) opt_newpin;
while (newpin == NULL) {
    u8 *newpin2;
    newpin = get_pin("Enter new PIN", pin_obj);
    if (pinpad_present && newpin == NULL)   {
        if (verbose)
            printf("New PIN value will be prompted with pinpad.\n");
        break;
    }
    ...
}
```

If `opt_newpin` is NULL and `pinpad_present` is true, `get_pin` returns NULL, and we break with `newpin == NULL`.

Then:
```c
r = sc_pkcs15_change_pin(p15card, pin_obj,
                pincode, pincode ? strlen((char *) pincode) : 0,
                newpin, newpin ? strlen((char *) newpin) : 0);
```

Then:
```c
if (opt_pin == NULL)
    free(pincode);
if (opt_newpin == NULL)
    free(newpin);
```

`free(NULL)` is fine. So the invalid-free must be inside `sc_pkcs15_change_pin` or in the card driver. Let me look at the `sc_pin_cmd` path more carefully. The crash is "Invalid-free" which means freeing a pointer that wasn't allocated by malloc. 

Let me look at the `sc_pkcs15_change_pin` function again. The key part is:

```c
if((!oldpin || !newpin)
        && (p15card->card->reader->capabilities & SC_READER_CAP_PIN_PAD
                || p15card->card->caps & SC_CARD_CAP_PROTECTED_AUTHENTICATION_PATH)) {
        data.flags |= SC_PIN_CMD_USE_PINPAD;
```

So if either pin is NULL and the reader has PIN pad capability, it sets `SC_PIN_CMD_USE_PINPAD`. Then `sc_pin_cmd` is called. If the card driver doesn't support `pin_cmd`, it falls back to the old interface. But with `SC_PIN_CMD_USE_PINPAD` set, it goes to the else branch:

```c
} else {
        sc_log(card->ctx,  "Use of pin pad not supported by card driver");
        r = SC_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED;
}
```

So it returns `SC_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED`. Then in `change_pin`:
```c
if (r == SC_ERROR_PIN_CODE_INCORRECT) {
    ...
} else if (r) {
    fprintf(stderr, "PIN code change failed: %s\n", sc_strerror(r));
    return 2;
}
```

It returns 2. So no crash there.

